  "interpretation": [
    "The first convolution already differs from the original PyTorch convolution by at most 3.814697265625e-6. Its output bytes are identical across the eager, portable and optimized native helpers.",
    "Batch normalization fed the exact original convolution still differs slightly: maximum 2.384185791015625e-7 for eager and 2.98023223876953125e-7 for both graph variants. This isolates additional BN evaluation-order differences, without attributing the entire later failure to them.",
    "The first-layer native ReLU payload matches the corresponding retained full-model boundary byte for byte in all three variants. The bounded probe reproduces that boundary exactly.",
    "Two diagnostic reciprocal/FMA evaluation orders did not eliminate the BN differences. Neither was installed in production.",
    "All fourteen isolated comparisons fit the unchanged stage budget. The later full-mask intermediate failures remain retained and unqualified; this experiment does not prove their complete causal chain or supply a numerical fix."
  ],
